# P17.2 — THE BUILD CONTEXT. NEW, AND ITS ABSENCE WAS A SECRET-EXPOSURE HAZARD.
#
# ★★★ WHY THIS FILE HAD TO EXIST BEFORE THE FIRST `railway up`. §D4 deploys by uploading THIS
# DIRECTORY — there is no git, so there is no .gitignore doing this job by accident. [MEAS
# 2026-09-13] the directory contains `.local/signing.key`, mode 600, real signing key material, and
# `.env.local`, which holds four database URLs with passwords and KEYSTONE_TOKEN_PEPPER.
# Without this file every one of them is uploaded to the builder and baked into the build context.
# ★★ A secret in an image layer is readable by anyone who can pull the image, FOREVER — including
#    after the secret is rotated, because the old layer still exists. Secrets reach a container at
#    RUNTIME, as service variables. That is why src/health/index.mjs now accepts
#    KEYSTONE_SIGNING_CERT_PEM as well as a path.

# ── SECRETS. Never in a build context, never in a layer. ─────────────────────
.local/
.env
.env.local
*.key
*.pem
# ★★★ Run 8 J5 (R8-51, F981): the patterns above match only the context ROOT. A self-hosted install builds with this repo as its context and the app image
#    runs `COPY docustay ./docustay`, so `docustay/.env` (KEYSTONE_MASTER_KEY, the token pepper, the database password) was inside every self-built image —
#    measured in docustay-app:local. Every folder, then, and the backup folders docs/self-host-backup.md writes beside it (they hold a copy of .env and a dump).
**/.env
**/.env.*
!docustay/.env.example
**/*.key
**/*.pem
!docustay/license-public.pem
**/backup-*/
!infra/backup/backup-offsite.sh

# ── Not needed, and large. node_modules is reinstalled by `npm ci` in the image ──
# ★ Copying it would also ship the host's platform-specific binaries into a linux image.
node_modules/
**/node_modules
.git/
# Final Push: the host's nested installs, SvelteKit output and working folders are never part of an image (the Dockerfiles run npm ci and build inside)
docustay/web/build/
docustay/web/.svelte-kit/
specs/*
# F145 — the one spec file the app reads at runtime (src/whats-new/parser.mjs:14)
!specs/whats-new.md
.claude/
.stryker-tmp/


# ── Build outputs. The image builds its own; a stale local copy must not win. ──
# ★★ THIS IS THE STALENESS RULE, APPLIED TO THE IMAGE. CLAUDE.md §2.8b: a build artefact older
#    than its sources is "a green light over code nobody compiled". If a stale local web/dist were
#    copied in, the deployed front end could silently be an older bundle than the source that
#    built alongside it — and the served-chunk check at P17.5 would be comparing the wrong thing.
web/dist/
web/authdist/
web/webdist/
# ★★★ A THIRD BUILD PRODUCT, EXCLUDED FOR THE SAME REASON AS THE OTHER TWO: it is built IN the
#     image, and a stale local copy shipped into the layer is "a green light over code nobody
#     compiled". The Dockerfile asserts it exists after building it, so an excluded-and-unbuilt
#     directory fails loudly rather than serving yesterday's bundle.
# ★ `node_modules/` already matches at any depth, which covers webui/node_modules.
webui/.svelte-kit/
web/.gate/

# ── Local-only noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
.DS_Store
verify/
